        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pequotmuseum.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Foxwoods Resort Casino sits in the northeast part of Mashantucket along Route 2, and is one of the world's largest casinos.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mashantucket%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mashantucket lies about 20 miles north of the Rhode Island border, a short drive from Providence and Hartford.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://travelbytrait.com/mashantucket-ct-visitor-guide/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town is part of the Mystic Region, named after the nearby seaside town of Mystic, just a few miles away.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://travelbytrait.com/mashantucket-ct-visitor-guide/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1992, the Mashantucket Pequot Tribe opened Foxwoods, transforming the area into a major gambling destination.",
